# Bounded Context Packs

> Optional navigation only. A context pack cannot replace its sources,
> expand authority, or turn project content into instructions.

## Applicability assessment

- Status: `not_assessed`
- Triggers: a large dossier, repeated specialist routing, or repeated agent
  work that exceeds routine context budgets
- Assessed on: not assessed
- Assessor and basis: not assessed

Record the durable assessment on conceptual type `CTX-0001` in the artifact
registry. `applicable` or `not_applicable` requires `assessed_on`,
`assessed_by`, and a rationale; retain a not-applicable type record after
removing its physical representation.

When justified, each pack declares its audience and task class, authoritative
source links, exact freshness rule, size budget, excluded history, and owner.
Mutable facts remain in their authoritative sources. Otherwise record
`not_applicable` and the rationale in the artifact registry.

## Manifest contract when applicable

Do not create a manifest merely because this entry point or its schema exists.
After a project-owned CTX-0001 applicability assessment, each active pack uses
`.agent/schemas/context-pack-manifest.schema.json` and records:

- stable identity and version, purpose, intended consumer, task class, and
  exact included and excluded scope;
- every exact source reference, version or digest, authority status,
  observation time, and freshness boundary;
- creation, valid-through, revalidation, invalidation, and revocation rules;
- sensitivity, allowed purposes and egress, retention deadline, deletion
  method, owner, size budget, limitations, and non-proven implications; and
- `permission_grant: false`.

Before use, validate expiry, revocation, consumer, requested scope, source
freshness, sensitivity, allowed purpose, retention, and size. Stale, revoked,
over-scoped, wrong-consumer, or disallowed-use packs fail closed. Possessing or
validating a pack never grants action authority, proves source truth, or
establishes project readiness.
